{"availability":"available","full":"ayenora/screen-loupe","name":"screen-loupe","description":"Native macOS screen loupe: a floating capture area mirrored live into a zoomable, pixel-sharp viewer","category":"Design","language":"Swift","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T07:53:07Z","updated":"2026-10-02T09:59:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ayenora.github.io/screen-loupe/","topics":["design-tools","developer-tools","macos","magnifier","metal","screencapturekit","swift"],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:13:48.094Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A small native macOS magnifier for designers and developers.","Place a Capture Area rectangle over any part of the screen and inspect it in a separate Viewer window. The Viewer shows the area in real time and supports:","A separate Screenshot studio takes exact, clean pictures — App Store and website screenshots, docs, bug reports: preset and custom pixel sizes, a timer, a backdrop of a colour, gradient or image seen on screen, one window alone with or without its shadow, and PNG, JPEG or HEIC output in sRGB or the display's colours, with no personal metadata."],"features":["pixel-sharp zoom that glides between levels, panning, and a window sized to the magnified area;","a crosshair on the real cursor, a freeze frame for transient states, and snapshots kept across launches to inspect later, linked to share one zoom and position;","a Color Meter (HEX, CSS, SwiftUI, AppKit, recent and favourite colours, WCAG contrast) and a pixel grid;","a corner ruler and a selection ruler in screen pixels, and the selection's size in pixels and points;","colour vision simulation: six modes over everything the Vi